{#- Drawn at 1366 px (the 12.9in iPad's long side in points) and exported
    at 2x, so the PNG is 2732 px — native for the largest iPad, and the
    wordmark stays vector-sharp because the browser draws it at that size
    rather than scaling a bitmap.

    Everything sits inside the middle 1024 px square. A 4:3 iPad shows a
    1024 x 1366 slice of this square in portrait and a 1366 x 1024 slice in
    landscape, so the centre square is the only part guaranteed to be on
    screen. The lock-screen clock sits in the top third in both
    orientations, so the mark sits slightly below centre to stay clear of
    it. -#}
